  "In-distribution gains: the largest gains (executed factory scenarios, real git sequences, agent sessions) are on sets built by the same generators as its training rows. On new kinds of actions the evidence is smaller: the fresh never-trained families (+1.6 points) and the neutral agent turns (AUROC level with Ekbasis-27B).",
  "\"Held-out\" git command types: the release protocol's held-out types are held out of the git-sandbox training rows, but Skopos' shell and git factory rows include them (the overlap audit's note); read the held-out rows as a weaker test than for Ekbasis-27B.",
  "Long chains in written-rule worlds: answering in one pass, its accuracy falls with the number of actions (86.8% over 1–20); a model that simulates step by step does better there at far higher cost. Use simulate (look when unsure) for long chains.",
